[1mbrigada init[0m · example.invalid/imported

[38;2;138;143;152mbrigada runs coding tasks on the agent CLIs you are signed in to. A foreman[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m(an agent) turns your request into a plan of tasks; workers (other agents)[0m
[38;2;138;143;152mwrite the code in their own git worktrees; your check command tests it; and[0m
[38;2;138;143;152man agent of a different model family reviews it. Four short steps follow.[0m
[38;2;138;143;152mNothing is written or started until you confirm at the end.[0m

[1m━━ Step 1 of 4 · agents[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  Each agent CLI below can work for brigada. For each one, pick the model it[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  should run, or leave it out. Reviews always go to a different model family[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  than the author's, so you need at least two families (e.g. claude + codex).[0m

