[1m━━ Step 3 of 4 · tasks at once[0m
  [38;2;138;143;152mEach running task is one agent CLI working in its own copy of the repo,
  plus your check command, so this is bounded by your machine. This one
  has 14 cores. Each CLI's account also gets its own limit (claude 3,
  codex 2, kimi 1, opencode 2, brigada's defaults, never above this
  number); change any of them later with brigada config.[0m
[1m    Tasks at once [0m[38;2;108;198;224m[4][0m[1m:[0m

[1m━━ Step 4 of 4 · how brigada tests the work[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  When an agent finishes a task, brigada runs one command in that task's[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  own copy of the repo (never in your working copy):[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m    passes (exit 0)  the work goes on to review by another model family[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m    fails            the work goes back to the agent, with the output[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  Use the command you run yourself to be sure nothing broke: tests,[0m
[38;2;138;143;152m  lint, type checks. Claude workers may run it too before handing in.[0m

  Found in this repo:
   ▸[38;2;108;198;224m 1[0m  [1muv run pytest[0m  [38;2;138;143;152mpytest, from uv.lock[0m  [38;2;108;198;224mdefault[0m
    [38;2;108;198;224m -[0m  no check       [38;2;138;143;152mwork goes straight to review; add one later[0m
